  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "The A-to-B dependency is per expert job",
      "items": [
        "The helper credits each job when this CTA finishes its A share. Each compute warp waits for the current B job to reach all 512 A units, then loads that job's intermediate rows into registers.",
        "There is no grid barrier between A and B. CTAs can reach B at different times. The global grid barrier appears after all B epilogues and before the final expert normalization and route combination."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What each memory boundary contains",
      "items": [
        "Phase A keeps the gate/up BF16 rounding before SiLU and multiplication, then writes BF16 inter. Phase B rounds down-projection values to BF16, applies the expert norm weights and stores FP32 y plus square sums.",
        "The final pass uses all 4096 features for each expert RMS denominator. It adds local routes in routing-slot order and writes BF16 [T,4096]. Four column segments per token distribute this pass."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Incumbent, not the parked readiness experiment",
      "items": [
        "This is the public607 integrated native source with DF, MFIN and MoE PDL disabled. Distributed ready flags and sentinel-based shortcuts are excluded.",
        "The arrows express dependencies. They do not assign durations to waits or arithmetic. Existing observer evidence does not yet qualify those internal costs."
      ]
    }
  ]
